Add a view switch between the classic Calculation screen and the new Calculation Center
in our Angular + PrimeNG app. Inspect the existing routes and components first, reuse
what exists, and avoid unrelated refactoring.

WHAT TO BUILD
- A text link with a swap icon. It must NOT look like a button: no background,
  no border, no shadow.
  - Classic Calculation page: "Switch to new Calculation Center"
  - Every Calculation Center page (card list and calculation detail): "Switch to classic view"
- Build it as one small reusable component, e.g. <app-view-switch [target]="'new' | 'classic'">,
  used on both screens.

PLACEMENT
- Top right of the page header, vertically centred with the page title.
- Same position on both screens, so users find it in the same place.

STYLE
- PrimeNG: <p-button [link]="true" icon="pi pi-arrow-right-arrow-left" iconPos="left">
  or a plain <a> styled the same way.
- Text: 13–14px, font-weight 600–700, primary blue (theme primary colour).
- Underline: a subtle dotted underline under the label only (not the icon),
  e.g. border-bottom: 1.5px dotted (primary at ~40% opacity).
- Hover: solid underline and slightly darker blue. Focus: visible focus ring.
- Spacing: 6–8px gap between icon and label. No padding box, no background.
- Tooltip (pTooltip, position bottom):
  - Classic page: "Run calculations with live readiness and progress"
  - New page: "Open the classic Calculation screen"

BEHAVIOUR
- Classic → new:
  - If a calculation is open in the classic screen (e.g. NET_INCOME_ETR, OCI),
    open the same calculation's detail page in the Calculation Center.
  - Otherwise open the Calculation Center card list (#/CALC_CENTER).
- New → classic:
  - From a calculation detail page, open that calculation in the classic screen.
  - From the card list, open the classic Calculation page.
- Use one shared mapping between classic calculation codes (NET_INCOME_ETR, OCI,
  ALLL_PULC, TCE, COC, Tax ETR) and Calculation Center calculation IDs, in both
  directions. If a calculation has no match, fall back to the target screen's
  landing page.
- If a calculation run is active in the new view, still allow switching. The run
  continues on the server; do not cancel anything.
- Use the words "new" and "classic" in the UI. Never use "old".

ACCESSIBILITY
- Use a real <a> or <button>, keyboard reachable, with aria-label matching the visible text.
- The icon is decorative (aria-hidden="true").

DONE WHEN
- The link appears in the same spot on the classic page, the Calculation Center
  card list and the calculation detail page.
- Each link routes correctly in both directions, including the same-calculation mapping.
- It looks like a link, not a button.
- Unit tests cover the mapping and both directions. Build and lint pass.
  Report what you ran.
